package com.vikash.bedtimestories.data

/** Longer retellings, written to be read aloud in about five to seven minutes. */
internal val LONG_ORIGINALS_A: Map<String, List<LP>> = mapOf(
    "moon-button" to listOf(
        LP("house hero", "One quiet night, the whole town was asleep. The streets were still, the gardens were dark, and only one little window was open. Behind it sat {name}, wide awake, looking up at the big round Moon."),
        LP("hero star", "The Moon was usually bright and smiling. But tonight the Moon looked sad. The soft, glowing coat it wore was flapping open, because one tiny silver button was missing from the front."),
        LP("hero sparkle", "“Moon,” whispered {name}, “why do you look so sad?” The Moon sighed a long, silvery sigh. “I dropped my button somewhere down below. Without it, my coat will not stay closed, and the night feels chilly.”"),
        LP("hero", "{name} thought about how it feels to be cold at night, with no blanket at all. That did not seem fair for anyone, not even the Moon. So {name} pulled on warm slippers and a cozy jumper."),
        LP("hero star", "“I will help you look,” said {name}. The Moon brightened just a little. “Thank you,” said the Moon. “I will shine my light on the path, so you can see where you are going.”"),
        LP("hero sparkle", "{name} tiptoed out of the door and into the garden. The grass was cool and damp. The flowers had closed up tight for the night. Everything smelled fresh and green, and the moonlight lay on the path like a ribbon."),
        LP("snail hero", "Halfway down the path, an old snail was sliding along, slow and steady, leaving a shiny trail behind. “Good evening, Mr Snail,” said {name} politely. “Have you seen a little silver button?”"),
        LP("snail", "The snail stopped and thought for a long time, the way snails do. “Hmm,” said the snail. “Hmmmm. Something round and shiny rolled past me a while ago. Roll, roll, roll it went, toward the pond.”"),
        LP("snail hero", "“Thank you so much,” said {name}. “You are very welcome,” said the snail. “I would come along, but I am rather slow. Off you go, and good luck.” {name} waved and hurried on."),
        LP("hero sparkle", "Down by the pond, the water was dark and smooth like glass. Reeds swayed gently. Somewhere a cricket sang chirp, chirp, chirp. And on a lily pad, something small was glinting in the moonlight."),
        LP("frog button", "It was a little green frog, holding the silver button up like a treasure. The frog turned it this way and that, watching it sparkle. “It is the prettiest thing I have ever found,” said the frog happily."),
        LP("frog button hero", "{name} knelt down at the edge of the pond and smiled gently. “It is very pretty,” said {name}. “But it belongs to the Moon. The Moon dropped it, and now the Moon is cold without it.”"),
        LP("frog button", "The frog looked at the button. Then the frog looked up at the Moon, shivering in that open coat. The frog thought for a moment, and then another moment, and then the frog nodded."),
        LP("frog hero button", "“Then the Moon should have it back,” said the frog, and held it out. “Thank you, little frog,” said {name}. “That was very kind. May I come back tomorrow and see your pond in the daytime?” “Yes, please,” croaked the frog."),
        LP("hero button sparkle", "{name} held the silver button up high, as high as {name} could reach. A long, soft moonbeam came sliding down from the sky, wrapped itself around the button, and carried it gently home."),
        LP("star sparkle", "The Moon fastened the button, and the glowing coat closed snugly at last. At once the Moon shone warm and bright, and all the stars twinkled a little brighter too, as if they were glad."),
        LP("hero house star", "{name} walked back up the moonlit path, past the sleepy snail, and in through the door. The slippers came off. The jumper came off. And {name} climbed into a soft, warm bed."),
        LP("hero~ star zzz", "“Thank you, {name},” whispered the Moon through the window. “Sleep well, kind friend.” The Moon kept watch all night long, warm and bright, while {name} drifted slowly, slowly off to sleep."),
    ),
    "owl-dark" to listOf(
        LP("owl oak", "Deep in the forest stood a tall pine tree. Near the very top, in a cozy hollow, lived a little owl named Pip. Pip had soft brown feathers, a fluffy chest, and two big round eyes."),
        LP("owl", "Now, owls are meant to love the night. Night is when owls wake up and fly and hoot. But Pip did not love the night. Not one bit. Pip was afraid of the dark."),
        LP("owl sun", "In the daytime, Pip was happy. The sun was warm and everything was easy to see. But when the sun went down and the shadows grew long, Pip hid under one wing and shivered."),
        LP("hero oak", "One evening, {name} was walking home through the forest. The sky was turning deep blue, and the path was soft with pine needles. It was very quiet. Then, from high above, came a tiny sound."),
        LP("hero owl", "“Hoo,” it went. Just a small, wobbly hoo. {name} stopped and looked up. “Who is there?” asked {name}. A little voice answered from the pine tree. “Only me. My name is Pip.”"),
        LP("hero owl", "“Hello, Pip,” said {name}. “Why are you hiding?” Pip peeked out from under one wing. “Because it is getting dark,” said the little owl, “and I am afraid of the dark.”"),
        LP("hero owl", "{name} did not laugh. {name} sat down on a mossy log right under the tree. “I know that feeling,” said {name} kindly. “Sometimes the dark feels big to me too.”"),
        LP("hero owl", "“Shall we look at the dark together?” asked {name}. “Things are easier with a friend.” Pip was quiet for a long moment. Then the little owl opened one round eye, just a crack."),
        LP("sparkle owl sparkle", "The first thing they saw was a tiny light. Blink. Then another. Blink, blink. Soon there were dozens of them, glowing softly between the trees. “Fireflies,” whispered {name}. “Like little lanterns.”"),
        LP("owl sparkle", "Pip opened the other eye. Then Pip leaned out of the hollow to look. “They are so pretty,” said Pip. “I never saw them before. I always had my eyes shut tight.”"),
        LP("hero owl", "“Now listen,” said {name}. They both held very still. Chirr, chirr, chirr, sang the crickets, slow and sleepy. Far away, a stream went trickle, trickle. The leaves whispered hush, hush, hush."),
        LP("owl star", "Then Pip looked up, past the branches, and gasped. The sky was full of stars, hundreds and hundreds, twinkling like scattered sugar. “Oh,” said Pip softly. “The dark is not empty at all. It is full of friends.”"),
        LP("hero owl", "“Would you like to try flying?” asked {name}. Pip’s feathers trembled. “I am still a little scared,” said Pip. “That is all right,” said {name}. “You can be scared and try anyway. I will be right here.”"),
        LP("owl oak", "Pip took a deep breath. Pip stretched out both soft wings. And then, with a little hop, Pip flew one small circle around the pine tree, and landed safely back in the hollow."),
        LP("owl star hero", "“I did it,” said Pip. “Shall I do a bigger one?” So Pip flew again, wider this time, out over the fireflies and under the stars. The stars seemed to twinkle a cheer. {name} clapped softly, so the forest would not wake."),
        LP("hero owl", "When Pip landed, the little owl was smiling. “Was I brave?” asked Pip. “Very brave,” said {name}. “Being brave does not mean you are never scared. It means you try anyway.”"),
        LP("owl hero house", "“Hoo, hoo,” sang Pip, loud and happy now. “Goodnight, {name}. Thank you.” {name} waved goodbye and walked the rest of the way home, under a sky that felt friendly and kind."),
        LP("hero~ owl star", "That night, {name} snuggled down in bed and looked out at the dark. It did not feel scary at all. Somewhere out there, Pip was flying under the stars. And slowly, softly, {name} fell asleep."),
    ),
    "sleepy-cloud" to listOf(
        LP("cloud sun", "High above the green hills, in a big blue sky, floated a little cloud named Nimbo. Nimbo was small and white and fluffy, like a scoop of whipped cream."),
        LP("cloud bird", "All day long, Nimbo had played. Nimbo raced the wind across the valley. Nimbo chased the birds around the treetops. Nimbo even made a funny shape, like a rabbit with very long ears."),
        LP("cloud sun", "But now the sun was sinking low, and the sky was turning gold and pink. Nimbo’s fluffy edges were drooping. Nimbo was very, very tired, and wanted to rest."),
        LP("cloud", "“I need somewhere soft to sleep,” yawned Nimbo. So the little cloud drifted along, looking for the perfect place. First, Nimbo floated over to a tall grey mountain."),
        LP("cloud", "Nimbo tried to settle on top. But the mountain was too pointy. Poke, poke, it went, right in Nimbo’s middle. “Ouch,” said Nimbo. “That will not do at all.”"),
        LP("cloud oak", "Next, Nimbo drifted down to a forest of big oak trees. Nimbo lay across the treetops. But the leaves were too tickly. Tickle, tickle, they went. Nimbo giggled and could not stop. “That will not do either.”"),
        LP("cloud", "Then Nimbo found a wide, shining lake. It looked smooth and calm. Nimbo floated down to lie on top of it. But splash, the lake was much too wet. “Oh dear,” sighed Nimbo. “Nothing is right.”"),
        LP("cloud bird", "A bird flew by on the way to its nest. “You look tired, little cloud,” chirped the bird. “I am,” said Nimbo. “But I am too wriggly and fidgety to rest anywhere.”"),
        LP("hero cloud", "Down below, on a grassy hill, {name} was lying on a soft blanket, watching the sky turn from pink to purple. {name} saw the little cloud wobbling about and smiled."),
        LP("hero cloud", "“You look sleepy, little cloud,” called {name}. “I am,” said Nimbo, “but I cannot settle down.” “I know a trick for that,” said {name}. “Try breathing slowly, like this.”"),
        LP("hero cloud", "{name} lay very still, rested two hands on a soft tummy, and breathed in, slowly, slowly, like smelling a flower. Then {name} breathed out, slowly, slowly, like blowing on warm soup. “In,” said {name}. “And out. In... and out.”"),
        LP("cloud", "Nimbo tried it. Nimbo breathed in, and grew round and soft and puffy. Nimbo breathed out, and drifted a little lower, gentle as a feather. “Oh,” said Nimbo. “That feels nice.”"),
        LP("cloud hero", "“Again,” said {name} softly. In... and out. In... and out. The wind grew quiet to listen. The birds stopped chattering and tucked their heads under their wings. Even the grass seemed to hold still."),
        LP("cloud", "In... and out. With every breath, Nimbo felt calmer and heavier and softer. The wriggles went away. The fidgets went away. Nimbo floated lower and lower, all the way down."),
        LP("cloud~ star", "At last, Nimbo settled gently on top of the round green hill, like a big white pillow. It was not too pointy. It was not too tickly. It was not too wet. It was just right."),
        LP("cloud~ star", "The first star came out to keep watch. “That is much better,” yawned the little cloud, and Nimbo’s fluffy edges curled up snug and cozy."),
        LP("hero house", "{name} yawned too, a big, wide yawn. {name} folded up the blanket and walked slowly home, across the hill, to a warm house and a cozy bed."),
        LP("house cloud~ zzz", "{name} lay down, closed both eyes, and breathed slowly. In... and out. In... and out. Outside the window, a small cloud was already dreaming. And soon, so was {name}."),
    ),
    "lantern-fish" to listOf(
        LP("fish", "Deep, deep down in the blue sea, where the water is cool and quiet, there was a busy little reef. Fish of every colour lived there, swimming in and out of the coral all day long."),
        LP("fish lumi fish", "Among them lived a small fish named Lumi. Lumi was not very big, and not very colourful. But Lumi had one special thing. On the tip of one fin glowed a tiny light, soft and gold."),
        LP("fish fish", "The other fish were very grand. Some had bright orange stripes. Some had long, floaty tails that swished like ribbons. Some had shiny blue scales that sparkled in the sunlight."),
        LP("lumi", "Lumi looked at them and then at the little glow. “Everyone else is so beautiful,” thought Lumi. “I only have this small light.” And Lumi often hid it behind a piece of coral."),
        LP("hero lumi", "One evening, {name} came sailing by in a small glass boat that could dive beneath the waves. Down, down it went, with bubbles floating up all around. Blub, blub, blub."),
        LP("hero lumi", "Through the glass, {name} saw a gentle golden glow peeking out from the coral. “What a lovely light,” said {name}. Lumi swam out shyly and blushed. “It is only small,” said the fish."),
        LP("hero lumi", "“Small things can be lovely,” said {name}. “Would you like to come exploring with me?” Lumi wiggled happily. Nobody had ever asked Lumi to go exploring before."),
        LP("lumi hero", "So off they went, the little boat and the little fish, side by side. They saw crabs dancing sideways. They saw sea stars resting on rocks. They saw seaweed waving hello, sway, sway, sway."),
        LP("turtle", "But as the sun went down far above, the water grew darker and darker. And out of the gloom came a small, sad sound. A baby turtle was swimming in circles, crying."),
        LP("turtle hero", "“What is wrong, little turtle?” asked {name}. “I swam too far,” sniffed the baby turtle. “Now it is dark, and I cannot find the way home to the reef. I cannot see anything at all.”"),
        LP("hero lumi", "{name} looked into the dark water. The boat had no lights. The stripy fish and the long-tailed fish had all gone home to sleep. Then {name} looked at Lumi and smiled."),
        LP("hero lumi", "“A small light is exactly what we need,” said {name}. Lumi felt nervous. “Me? But my light is so tiny.” “Tiny is enough,” said {name}. “You only need to see a little way at a time.”"),
        LP("lumi turtle", "Lumi took a deep breath, as deep as a small fish can. Then Lumi swam to the front and held up that little fin. The glow shone gold in the dark water, warm and steady."),
        LP("lumi turtle", "“Follow me,” said Lumi bravely. The baby turtle paddled close behind, and {name} steered the glass boat after them. Swish went the turtle. Glow went Lumi. Blub went the boat."),
        LP("lumi turtle whale~", "Past the waving seaweed they went. Past the quiet rocks. Past a great big whale, sleeping peacefully and snoring long, low snores. Very, very quietly, they tiptoed by."),
        LP("lumi turtle", "At last they saw the coral of the reef. And there was the baby turtle’s family, waiting with open flippers. “You are home,” they cried, and wrapped their little one in a big turtle hug."),
        LP("turtle lumi hero", "“Thank you,” said the turtle family to Lumi. Lumi’s light glowed brighter than ever. “Your light is not small at all,” said {name}. “It is just the right size to help.”"),
        LP("lumi~ hero", "Lumi glowed all the way home and curled up in the coral, never wanting to hide that light again. And {name} sailed the little glass boat back up, up, up, through the bubbles, to the surface."),
        LP("hero~ star zzz", "Soon {name} was tucked up in bed, warm and sleepy. A little night-light glowed softly in the corner, gold like Lumi’s fin. And {name} smiled, and closed both eyes, and drifted off to sleep."),
    ),
    "bear-honey" to listOf(
        LP("bear sun", "At the edge of a sunny meadow lived a big brown bear named Bruno. Bruno had soft fur, a round tummy, and a nose that could sniff out sweet things from very far away."),
        LP("bear honey", "One bright morning, Bruno’s nose twitched. Sniff, sniff. Something smelled wonderful. Bruno followed the smell all the way to a hollow log, and inside was the biggest pot of honey in the whole meadow."),
        LP("bear honey", "It was golden and sticky and shining. “Mine,” said Bruno, hugging the pot close. “All mine.” And Bruno carried it far away, up to the very top of a tall green hill."),
        LP("hero rabbit mouse", "Down in the meadow, {name} was picking flowers with a fluffy rabbit and a little grey mouse. There were yellow buttercups and white daisies, and they were making a long flower chain together."),
        LP("mouse rabbit", "The mouse lifted a tiny nose. Sniff, sniff. “Oh,” said the mouse. “That honey smells wonderful.” “It does,” said the rabbit, licking lips. “I wonder if Bruno would share.”"),
        LP("hero bear honey", "{name} waved up the hill. “Hello, Bruno!” But Bruno only hugged the pot tight and turned away, so they could not even see it. The mouse’s whiskers drooped a little."),
        LP("bear honey", "At the top of the hill, Bruno dipped in a big paw and licked it. Sweet. Then another pawful. Very sweet. Then another. The honey was delicious, just as Bruno had hoped."),
        LP("bear honey", "But something felt wrong. The hilltop was very quiet. There was no one to talk to. There was no one to say, “Isn’t this yummy?” The wind blew, and Bruno felt a little lonely."),
        LP("hero rabbit mouse", "Down below, {name} and the others had spread out a picnic blanket. They were laughing together. The rabbit told a silly joke, and the mouse laughed so hard, the mouse fell over."),
        LP("bear", "Bruno listened to the laughter drifting up the hill. Ha ha ha. Tee hee hee. Bruno looked down at the sticky paws and the big pot. Somehow the honey did not taste quite so sweet anymore."),
        LP("hero bear", "Then {name} noticed Bruno sitting all alone. “I think Bruno is lonely,” said {name}. “I will go and see.” So {name} climbed the hill, step by step, until the top."),
        LP("hero bear honey", "{name} sat down beside the bear. Bruno looked worried. “Have you come to take my honey?” “No,” said {name} gently. “I have come to say hello. You look a little sad up here by yourself.”"),
        LP("hero bear honey", "“We have warm bread down there,” said {name}, “fresh and soft. But we have nothing to put on it. And you have honey, but no one to enjoy it with. I wonder what would happen if we put them together?”"),
        LP("bear honey", "Bruno looked at the pot. Then Bruno looked down at the picnic, at the rabbit and the mouse, waving with friendly faces. Bruno thought for a long time. Then the bear stood up."),
        LP("bear honey hero", "Slowly, carefully, Bruno carried the honey all the way down the hill. Step, step, step. {name} walked alongside. And when they reached the blanket, Bruno set the pot right in the middle."),
        LP("rabbit honey bear mouse", "Everyone had honey on warm bread. The rabbit had a big slice. The mouse had a tiny one. Bruno had a huge one. They laughed and talked and licked their sticky fingers, and the honey tasted twice as sweet."),
        LP("bear hero star", "When the sky turned dark and the first stars came out, Bruno walked {name} home along the meadow path. The crickets were singing, and the air smelled of flowers."),
        LP("bear hero house", "“Sharing made my honey smaller,” said the bear, “but it made my evening bigger.” {name} smiled. “Goodnight, Bruno.” “Goodnight, {name},” said the bear, with a big, warm, honey-sweet hug."),
        LP("hero~ bear~ zzz", "{name} climbed into bed, full and happy, and smiled all the way to sleep. And far away at the edge of the meadow, Bruno curled up too, dreaming of picnics with friends."),
    ),
    "snail-race" to listOf(
        LP("oak sun", "At the bottom of a big garden stood an old oak tree, with wide branches and roots like knobbly fingers. Every evening, as the sun went down, the garden animals had a race to it."),
        LP("rabbit squirrel", "“Ready, steady, go!” And off they went. The rabbit zoomed, hop, hop, hop, ears flapping. The squirrel zipped, scurry, scurry, tail bouncing. They reached the oak tree in no time at all."),
        LP("snail", "And Shelly the snail came last. Every single time. Shelly slid along, slow and steady, carrying a little swirly shell. By the time Shelly reached the oak, the others had already gone home."),
        LP("snail", "One evening, Shelly stopped in the middle of the path and sighed a small snail sigh. “It is no use,” said Shelly. “I will never win. I will always, always be last.”"),
        LP("hero snail", "Just then, {name} came walking across the garden and saw the little snail looking sad. “Hello, Shelly,” said {name}. “What is the matter?”"),
        LP("snail hero", "“I wish I were fast,” said Shelly. “Like the rabbit and the squirrel. I am too slow for everything.” {name} knelt down in the soft grass, so snail and friend were face to face."),
        LP("snail hero", "“May I walk at your speed tonight?” asked {name}. “I would like to see what you see.” Shelly blinked in surprise. Nobody had ever wanted to walk slowly before. “All right,” said Shelly."),
        LP("snail hero", "So they set off together, very slowly. {name} took tiny steps, one at a time. Step... and step... and step. Shelly slid along beside, and for once, Shelly was not left behind."),
        LP("snail sparkle hero", "The first thing they saw was a spider, finishing a silver web between two flowers. Round and round the spider went, spinning thread as fine as hair. The web shone in the last light like lace."),
        LP("sparkle snail", "Next they saw dewdrops resting on the blades of grass. Each one was round and clear, and inside each one, a tiny moon was shining. “Look,” whispered Shelly. “Hundreds of little moons.”"),
        LP("snail hero", "Then they smelled something sweet. The night flowers were opening, one by one, their pale petals unfolding slowly, slowly. “They only open in the evening,” said Shelly. “Most animals rush right past.”"),
        LP("rabbit snail", "Just then, the rabbit came hopping back. “Why are you so slow?” called the rabbit. “The race is over!” Then the rabbit saw the silver web, and the dewdrop moons, and stopped."),
        LP("rabbit snail", "“Oh,” whispered the rabbit, sniffing the night flowers. “I have hopped down this path a hundred times. I never noticed any of this.” The rabbit’s ears went soft and still."),
        LP("squirrel snail", "Then the squirrel came scurrying back to see what everyone was looking at. “What is it?” asked the squirrel. “Shh,” said Shelly. “Look slowly.” And the squirrel looked, and smiled."),
        LP("snail hero rabbit squirrel", "One by one, all the garden animals came back and walked slowly too. Nobody zoomed. Nobody zipped. It was the longest race the garden had ever had, and the most beautiful one."),
        LP("oak snail hero", "They all reached the old oak tree together, under a sky full of stars. “Who won?” asked the squirrel. Everyone looked at Shelly. “Slow is not last,” said {name}. “Slow is how you see everything.”"),
        LP("oak snail~ rabbit~", "Shelly’s shell glowed with happiness. The rabbit curled up between the roots. The squirrel climbed into a cozy nest. And Shelly tucked in, snug inside that little swirly shell."),
        LP("hero~ house zzz", "{name} walked home slowly, slowly, noticing every star. Then {name} climbed into bed, slowly, slowly, and let both eyes close, slowly, slowly. And everyone in the garden went to sleep."),
    ),
)
